# * balance report links with --base-url

# ** 1. Column headings link to the register for the column's period, as a
# period expression that reads back as the same span: a week is written
# out with its exclusive end date, not as an ISO week name.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

2025-01-22 b
  assets:cash  20
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -W -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01-13\.\.2025-01-20">2025-W03</
>= 0

# ** 2. The heading keeps its display form; only the link's term changes.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

2025-02-20 b
  assets:cash  20
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -M --period-titles=dates -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01">2025-01-01\.\.2025-01-31</
>= 0

# ** 3. A span that is not a calendar period keeps its last day: the
# heading shows the inclusive end date, the term the exclusive one.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

2025-02-20 b
  assets:cash  20
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -M -p 2025-01-15..2025-03-01 -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=date:2025-01-15\.\.2025-02-15">2025-01-15\.\.2025-02-14</
>= 0

# ** 4. The same term in the tidy layout's period column.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -W --layout=tidy -O html --base-url ''
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:cash\+date:2025-01-13\.\.2025-01-20">2025-W03</
>= 0

# ** 5. An inacct: term in the query is not carried into the links, which
# name their own account.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -O html --base-url '' inacct:assets
> /<a href="register\?q=inacct:assets:cash">assets:cash</
>= 0

# ** 6. Without --base-url, no links.
<
2025-01-15 a
  assets:cash  10
  income

$ hledger -f- bal -W -O html
> !/<a href/
>= 0
